By hand, afterwards:
  cargo test --features semantic --test all     (2.21 GB free)  ->  Finished; **561 passed**. It links alone; in the matrix it
      links beside six other feature sets' artifacts.
  cargo build --examples --all-features          (the same step, alone)  -> see eval.md: it is the disk, and
      `cargo check --examples --all-features` is what holds the code side of it.

The two warnings in every step are the same two: ``bevy_siren` (example "quick_start")` and `(example "mixer")` each generate
one, and they are the macOS linker message `ld: __eh_frame section too large` — a Bevy debug binary's unwinding table, not
a warning in this crate's code (`cargo clippy -D warnings` is green).
